<Docs slug="select-a-photo">
  <p>
    Highlight a photo in the grid and press <kbd>Enter</kbd> or
    <kbd>Space</kbd> to open it full size in the editor. From there:
  </p>

  <ul class="lp-article-list">
    <li>
      <kbd>&larr;</kbd> / <kbd>&rarr;</kbd> step to the previous or next photo
      without leaving the editor, so you can move through a burst at full size.
    </li>
    <li>
      <kbd>Esc</kbd> or <kbd>G</kbd> goes back to the grid, and <kbd>E</kbd>
      opens the highlighted photo again.
    </li>
    <li>
      <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>0</kbd> fits the photo to the window,
      <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>1</kbd> shows it at 1:1, and
      <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>=</kbd> / <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>-</kbd> zoom in and
      out in steps, as do <kbd>&uarr;</kbd> / <kbd>&darr;</kbd> in smaller
      ones. Scrolling zooms at the pointer. Drag, or hold <kbd>Space</kbd> and
      drag, to pan; <kbd>Shift</kbd>+scroll and <kbd>Alt</kbd>+scroll pan
      sideways and up and down.
    </li>
    <li>
      <kbd>R</kbd> starts a crop (<kbd>Enter</kbd> applies it, <kbd>Esc</kbd>
      cancels), and <kbd>Y</kbd> shows the original and your edit side by
      side — the quickest way to check you have not gone too far.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Once a photo is open, the tabs on the right are where you
    <a href="/docs/adjust.html">adjust the settings</a>.
  </p>
</Docs>
